idate A), refer to discussion, use explicit facts, explain implications.\n\nWe can say: The lack of evidence on B's attention to detail and decision quality means we cannot fully assess his suitability; given his known crew cooperation issues, and the missing data, we remain with Candidate A. Also note that D's crew cooperation concerns and unknown communication also problematic. So we keep A.\n\nThus public message: I remain with Candidate A, because B's missing data on attention and decision quality, combined with his interpersonal issues, make him less reliable. Also D's issues. C also has communication issues. So A still best.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate A."}
